### ProxyPunishments service — runnable request collection.
### Works in IntelliJ IDEA and in VS Code with the REST Client extension.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up --build

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = dev-local-token
@player = 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
@alt = 22222222-3333-4444-5555-666666666666
@admin = 99999999-8888-7777-6666-555555555555
@address = 203.0.113.7

### Health — the only endpoint that needs no token
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Metrics — everything under the proxypunishments. prefix: punishments issued and lifted by kind,
### cache hit ratio, repository timings, Redis invalidations published and received, webhook deliveries
GET {{host}}/actuator/prometheus
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Register a player so names can be resolved (local mode only)
### "ip" is optional; it is what makes alt detection possible and is validated as a literal address
POST {{host}}/api/v1/known-players
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uuid": "{{player}}",
  "login": "Steve",
  "ip": "{{address}}"
}

### Register a second account seen from the same address
POST {{host}}/api/v1/known-players
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uuid": "{{alt}}",
  "login": "Alex",
  "ip": "{{address}}"
}

### Resolve a name to a UUID
GET {{host}}/api/v1/lookup?name=steve
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Issue a permanent ban
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "BAN",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "griefing spawn"
}

### Issue a 7-day ban
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "BAN",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "chat abuse",
  "durationSeconds": 604800
}

### Issue a 1-hour mute — the ban above stays in force
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "MUTE",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "spamming chat",
  "durationSeconds": 3600
}

### Issue a permanent IP ban — playerUuid records whose connection triggered it
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "IP_BAN",
  "ipAddress": "{{address}}",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "ban evasion"
}

### Issue an IP ban against a bare address — playerUuid may be the nil UUID
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "kind": "IP_BAN",
  "ipAddress": "198.51.100.9",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "open proxy",
  "durationSeconds": 604800
}

### Record a warning — log only, never active
POST {{host}}/api/v1/warnings
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "minor spam"
}

### The ban currently in force (404 when the player is clean; kind defaults to BAN)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}/active
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### The mute currently in force
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}/active?kind=MUTE
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Active bans, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments?kind=BAN&limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Active mutes, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments?kind=MUTE&limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### The IP ban currently in force for an address (404 when the address is clean)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/ip/{{address}}/active
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Active IP bans, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments?kind=IP_BAN&limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Alts — other accounts last seen from this player's address, most recent first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/players/{{player}}/alts?limit=20
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Punishment history — bans, mutes, IP bans and warnings together
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}/history?limit=20&offset=0
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Lift the ban
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}?kind=BAN
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "liftedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "liftedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "appeal accepted"
}

### Lift the mute
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}?kind=MUTE
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "liftedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "liftedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "cooled down"
}

### Lift the IP ban
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/ip/{{address}}
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "liftedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "liftedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "shared connection"
}

### Rejected: no token
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/{{player}}/active

### Rejected: limit above the maximum
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments?limit=1000000
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Rejected: unknown kind
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments?kind=KICK
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Rejected: IP_BAN without an address
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "IP_BAN",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "ban evasion"
}

### Rejected: the address is not an address
GET {{host}}/api/v1/punishments/ip/definitely-not-an-ip/active
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Cross-node invalidation — with proxypunishments.redis.enabled=true this ban is announced on the
### invalidation channel, so every other service replica and every proxy drops its cached answer at
### once instead of waiting out its TTL. Watch it with: docker compose exec redis redis-cli \
###   subscribe proxypunishments.invalidations
POST {{host}}/api/v1/punishments
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerUuid": "{{player}}",
  "kind": "BAN",
  "issuedByUuid": "{{admin}}",
  "issuedByName": "Admin",
  "reason": "cross-node invalidation demo"
}
